+// HOST COMMIT CACHE (2026-10-02, Saints Reborn perf). Guest heaps with pages >= the host page size are views
+// of one SEC_RESERVE mapping; the host never decommits them (Decommit/Release only change the page table), so a
+// page committed once with read-write access stays committed read-write until this heap changes its host
+// protection (BaseHeap::Protect, protect_on_release). The game's job arenas decommit and recommit ~300 MB/s;
+// each recommit called VirtualAlloc(MEM_COMMIT) again - a no-op syscall under the global lock. Remember the
+// pages and skip it. Virtual heaps only. File "host_commit_cache.off" next to the exe = old behaviour.
